<title>CHINA: China southwest Guizhou gold output rises.</title>
<headline>China southwest Guizhou gold output rises.</headline>
<dateline>BEIJING 1996-09-17</dateline>
<text>
<p>Gold output in China's southwestern Guizhou province was 35,500 ounces in the first eight months of this year, exceeding the annual planned target, the Xinhua news agency said on Tuesday.</p>
<p>Gold output was expected to exceed 55,000 ounces this year, an increase of 40 percent over 1995, it said.</p>
<p>It gave no other details.</p>
</text>
